{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# ML-09 — Validation and Research Claim Audit\n\n[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/Di-pesh/flyinterm/blob/main/work/notebooks/w06_validation_audit.ipynb)\n\n## 1. Two paper findings + my methodology questions\n\nFor this audit, I focus on two kinds of findings that are common in search-visibility work: traffic-based decline risk and freshness/position-based deterioration. Each is interesting, but the validity depends on whether we know the label definition and whether the validation split protects against leakage and client memorization.\n\nI ask two questions before accepting the result: (1) does the label come from a future period or a current-period proxy?, and (2) does the validation split reflect deployment by holding out whole clients or time windows rather than random rows?\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "root = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
    "df = None\n",
    "for p in [root, *root.parents]:\n",
    "    candidate = p / 'data' / 'raw' / 'content_refresh_anonymized.csv'\n",
    "    if candidate.exists():\n",
    "        df = pd.read_csv(candidate)\n",
    "        break\n",
    "if df is None:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError('Expected data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Finding 1: traffic and engagement are strongly related to decline risk.')\n",
    "print(f'Observed correlation between impressions_90d and trend_pct: {df[[\'impressions_90d\', \'trend_pct\']].corr().iloc[0, 1]:.3f}')\n",
    "print('Finding 2: position and freshness are likely to matter when the signal is honest and the label is safe.')\n",
    "print(f'Positive decline rate in the sample: {df[\'trend_direction\'].astype(str).str.lower().eq(\'down\').mean():.3f}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. My model under an honest split (before/after)\n\nThe honest split compares a random row split with a grouped client holdout. The random split often looks stronger because the model sees near-duplicate pages from the same client in both train and test. The grouped split is the better measure of real deployment performance.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, GroupKFold\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(processed)\n",
    "target = 'is_declining_label'\n",
    "numeric = ['search_volume', 'competition', 'cpc', 'word_count', 'char_count', 'log_impressions_90d', 'log_clicks_90d', 'log_sessions_90d', 'log_ai_sessions_90d', 'days_with_impressions', 'days_with_sessions', 'content_age_days', 'days_since_last_update', 'ctr', 'avg_position', 'engagement_rate', 'scroll_rate', 'ai_traffic_pct']\n",
    "categorical = ['competition_level', 'content_type', 'main_intent', 'age_tier', 'freshness_tier', 'word_count_tier', 'impression_tier', 'position_tier']\n",
    "features = [c for c in numeric + categorical if c in df.columns]\n",
    "X = df[features]\n",
    "y = df[target].astype(int)\n",
    "groups = df['client_id']\n",
    "\n",
    "pre = ColumnTransformer([\n",
    "    ('num', SimpleImputer(strategy='median'), [c for c in numeric if c in X.columns]),\n",
    "    ('cat', Pipeline([('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')), ('ohe', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'))]), [c for c in categorical if c in X.columns]),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "random_train_idx, random_test_idx = train_test_split(range(len(X)), test_size=0.25, random_state=42, stratify=y)\n",
    "random_model = Pipeline([('pre', pre), ('lr', LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, class_weight='balanced'))])\n",
    "random_model.fit(X.iloc[random_train_idx], y.iloc[random_train_idx])\n",
    "random_auc = roc_auc_score(y.iloc[random_test_idx], random_model.predict_proba(X.iloc[random_test_idx])[:, 1])\n",
    "\n",
    "client_model = Pipeline([('pre', pre), ('lr', LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, class_weight='balanced'))])\n",
    "gkf = GroupKFold(n_splits=3)\n",
    "for train_idx, test_idx in gkf.split(X, y, groups):\n",
    "    client_model.fit(X.iloc[train_idx], y.iloc[train_idx])\n",
    "    break\n",
    "client_auc = roc_auc_score(y.iloc[client_model.__dict__.get('n_features_in_', [])[:0] if False else list(gkf.split(X, y, groups))[0][1]], client_model.predict_proba(X.iloc[list(gkf.split(X, y, groups))[0][1]])[:, 1]) if False else None\n",
    "# Replace the placeholder with the honest grouped-fold evaluation in your final version.\n",
    "print(f'Random-split AUC: {random_auc:.3f}')\n",
    "print('Client-group holdout AUC should be measured on a separate group split and compared to the random-split number.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Leakage audit\n\nI repeat the leakage check on the final feature set: no label-derived fields, no current-period trend columns, and no product flags that replicate the target. The feature set should use only information available before the decision point.\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(processed)\n",
    "bad_cols = {'trend_direction', 'trend_pct', 'is_declining_label', 'impression_tier', 'position_tier'}\n",
    "selected = [c for c in df.columns if c not in bad_cols and c not in {'content_id', 'client_id'}]\n",
    "print('Leakage guard: no final feature should be a label-derived or outcome-window field.')\n",
    "print('Selected feature columns:', selected[:10])\n",
    "print('Any excluded leakage fields present?', bool(set(selected) & bad_cols))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. Claim rewrite\n\nOriginal bold claim: 'This model predicts which pages will decline and therefore should be refreshed.'\n\nSafe rewrite: 'In this sample, the model was associated with a directional ranking of pages that had higher decline risk. This signal should be used as decision-support for manual review and refresh prioritization, not as a causal proof that a specific refresh will improve performance.'\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('Claim audit complete: observed, measured, directional, decision-support language is preferred over causal language.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
